# Shared types error sentences.
error-hash-not-sha256-hex = That fingerprint isn't valid. It must be exactly 64 lower-case letters and digits.
error-id-memory-ref-invalid = That memory reference isn't valid. Choose it from the list instead of typing it.
error-id-not-uuidv7 = That name isn't valid. Use the one ordin gave you, without changing it.
error-input-location-invalid = The location of that input isn't valid or is too long. Check it and try again.
error-input-name-invalid = That name isn't valid. Check its length and characters and try again.
error-input-version-invalid = The version of that input isn't valid or is too long. Check it and try again.
error-num-not-decimal = That isn't a valid number. Use digits with an optional decimal point.
error-srv-bad-cursor = The list position is no longer valid. Go back to the start of the list and try again.
error-text-control-char = That text contains a character that isn't allowed. Remove it and try again.
error-ts-not-rfc3339-ms-utc = That date and time isn't valid. Check it and try again.
error-yaml-feature-refused = That file uses a feature ordin doesn't accept. Keep it to plain settings.
error-yaml-malformed = That file isn't laid out correctly. Check it for repeated names, deep nesting or missing parts.
error-yaml-too-large = That file is too large. Shorten it and try again.
